# Plane -3y + 4z = -1, tilted to pass exactly through one edge of clay_unit_cube.
#
# Regression test for Bug 1 (local vs global vertex index).
# The bottom-front edge of the unit cube runs from (-1,-1,-1) to (1,-1,-1).
# Both endpoints satisfy -3(-1) + 4(-1) = 3 - 4 = -1.
# No other cube vertex lies on this plane (checked: remaining 6 vertices give -7 or 7 or 1).
#
# The intersection of this knife with the bottom and front faces of the cube
# will have endpoints that are exactly at the two edge vertices, triggering the
# "this intersection point IS an existing clay mesh vertex" code path in
# convertIntersectionToIpoints.  Two clay faces share this edge so both vertices
# will be identified as clay-mesh vertices simultaneously.

v -3 -3 -2.5
v  3 -3 -2.5
v  3  3  2.0
v -3  3  2.0

f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
